course: dictionary
lesson: 5958
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word «mate» is a good example. In «He's my mate», it means friend. In a science lesson about animals, it means a partner that an animal has babies with.
explain: Read the words around it. «Cheers, mate!» is friendly chat in Britain and Australia, so it means something like thanks, not a pal you share a bike with. A first mate on a pirate ship is an officer, not a friend. The clues show you which meaning fits.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. If «Then she misses her mate's party» still makes sense with friend, you have the right meaning. If a sentence about birds singing to attract a mate stops making sense with friend, try the partner meaning instead.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Mate» means friend in everyday British, Australian, New Zealand and Irish speech, as in «He's my mate».
fact: «Mate» can also mean a person you share something with, as in «classmate», «teammate» and «flatmate».
fact: In science, a mate is the partner an animal finds so they can have babies together.
fact: In chess, «mate» is short for «checkmate», which ends the game.
exercise: «Then she misses her mate's party because she has to mind the boys, and she's gutted.» What does mate mean here? | *A friend | An officer on a ship | The end of a game of chess | A partner that an animal has babies with
exercise: In a science lesson, birds sing to attract a mate. What does mate mean here? | A game of chess | *A partner that a bird has babies with | An officer on a ship | A friend who sings with you
exercise: In «my flatmate», what does mate mean? | A pet | A toy | A wild animal | *A person you share something with
test: «Cheers, mate!» is said in Britain. What does mate mean here? | A hard test at school | A type of ship | *A friendly word, like hello or thanks
test: In chess, «mate» ends the game. What is the short word for it? | *Checkmate | Checkpoint | Teammate | Classmate
exam: Lena reads: «The bird sang to attract a mate, then it built a nest.» Which meaning of mate fits, and how do you know? | *A partner to have babies with, because the sentence is about a bird and a nest | A friend, because birds have friends at school | A chess move, because birds play games | An officer on a ship, because birds sail
